1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,100
[The D Dorm]

2
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:06,530
How ironic that

3
00:00:06,910 --> 00:00:09,860
we searched the entire dorm
for Grandma Gaysorn's relative,

4
00:00:09,930 --> 00:00:12,410
only for the photo to come from Ms. Danis.

5
00:00:12,430 --> 00:00:15,130
This is straight out of
a one31 evening drama.

6
00:00:15,710 --> 00:00:17,010
- How so?
- Well...

7
00:00:17,330 --> 00:00:19,450
it's that plot where parents
look for their missing child.

8
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:21,500
Or the child is searching for their parents.

9
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:22,940
They kept missing each other.

10
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:24,540
They almost met, yet never did.

11
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:25,570
Oh, in some dramas,

12
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:29,780
a blind father has to search for
his missing wife and child.

13
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:32,130
Yeah, I really love that kinda plot.

14
00:00:32,150 --> 00:00:33,590
I've always wanted to give that role a try.

15
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:38,310
My child.

16
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:39,140
Dear.

17
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:39,820
Hey.

18
00:00:39,830 --> 00:00:40,970
- Hey...
- Whoa.

19
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:41,860
Hey.

20
00:00:42,230 --> 00:00:43,230
Hey,

21
00:00:43,870 --> 00:00:45,420
is this my child?

22
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:46,730
How did you grow up

23
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:48,530
to have skin as bumpy as the Moon's, dear?

24
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:49,450
Ugh!

25
00:00:50,220 --> 00:00:51,740
Why are you playing along with him?

26
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:53,810
Ugh...

27
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:56,300
Where's Ms. Danis?

28
00:00:56,480 --> 00:00:57,520
Why isn't she here yet?

29
00:00:57,740 --> 00:00:58,740
Her phone was dead when I called.

30
00:00:58,760 --> 00:00:59,780
I didn't even get to talk to her.

31
00:01:00,610 --> 00:01:02,140
I’ll go check for you.

32
00:01:05,330 --> 00:01:07,180
There are no cars in the parking lot.

33
00:01:07,270 --> 00:01:09,330
Maybe she is coming here by taxi.

34
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:15,830
Maybe she parked under the dorm.

35
00:01:16,330 --> 00:01:17,340
Ugh!

36
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:17,980
What?

37
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:19,539
Stop popping in and out already.

38
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:20,510
I'm dizzy.

39
00:01:22,539 --> 00:01:23,300
Oh!

40
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:27,340
I meant,

41
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:31,120
I've been going back and forth
trying to picture

42
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:32,390
what Grandma Gaysorn looks like,

43
00:01:32,570 --> 00:01:34,660
and it's making me dizzy.

44
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:35,880
- I see.
- Yes.

45
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:37,340
So that's how it is.

46
00:01:37,530 --> 00:01:38,640
Hey, Dobby.

47
00:01:38,650 --> 00:01:39,120
Huh?

48
00:01:39,130 --> 00:01:41,210
When you talked to Danis,

49
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:43,000
she said that the box she was carrying

50
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:44,410
belonged to the director of the orphanage.

51
00:01:44,810 --> 00:01:45,880
Is there a chance

52
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:48,220
that the orphanage director
is Grandma Gaysorn?

53
00:01:49,979 --> 00:01:51,020
I do not think so.

54
00:01:51,390 --> 00:01:52,539
She said that

55
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:54,700
the director's name was Nampetch.

56
00:01:56,620 --> 00:01:58,810
Her orphanage director is named Nampetch.

57
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:01,030
Where?

58
00:02:01,330 --> 00:02:02,680
Where is Grandma Gaysorn's photo?

59
00:02:02,710 --> 00:02:04,610
Let me see the photo you said I dropped.

60
00:02:04,630 --> 00:02:05,410
Here.

61
00:02:07,430 --> 00:02:08,259
Huh?

62
00:02:08,340 --> 00:02:10,639
Is this the photo?
I can't even see her face.

63
00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:11,740
You don't remember?

64
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:12,760
Hey,

65
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:15,340
are you sure
I was the one who dropped this?

66
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:17,110
Mr. Disney told me that

67
00:02:17,329 --> 00:02:19,140
as he was walking up to the fourth floor,

68
00:02:19,170 --> 00:02:21,060
this was the photo

69
00:02:21,070 --> 00:02:22,180
that fell past him.

70
00:02:22,630 --> 00:02:25,500
When he got to the fourth floor,
he saw you carrying a cardboard box,

71
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:27,540
so you probably dropped it.

72
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:29,220
Hey, Ms. Danis, I think...

73
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,620
you should call the director

74
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:32,660
and ask her if this photo is hers.

75
00:02:35,930 --> 00:02:37,520
It's probably too late to call her now.

76
00:02:37,540 --> 00:02:38,190
- Huh?
- Huh?

77
00:02:40,630 --> 00:02:41,630
Don't tell me...

78
00:02:42,060 --> 00:02:43,180
Did she pass away?

79
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:45,530
She already went to bed.

80
00:02:45,550 --> 00:02:46,430
- Oh.
- Ugh.

81
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:48,500
Then why did you look so worried?

82
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:49,850
Well, even if she's awake,

83
00:02:49,870 --> 00:02:51,910
she wouldn't be able to
give you any answers.

84
00:02:52,110 --> 00:02:52,930
Huh?

85
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:55,530
Lately, I've been visiting her more often

86
00:02:56,130 --> 00:02:57,420
because she has Alzheimer's disease.

87
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:58,700
She can't remember much.

88
00:02:58,720 --> 00:02:59,530
Oh...

89
00:03:00,140 --> 00:03:01,140
See?

90
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:03,340
This is definitely
a one31 evening drama plot.

91
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:05,940
She has memory loss
due to Alzheimer's disease.

92
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:08,370
Given the chance,
I'd like to work with Boyd Kosiyabong.

93
00:03:09,010 --> 00:03:10,010
Boy Takonkiet.

94
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:11,840
I have to get this role.

95
00:03:12,630 --> 00:03:13,720
My child.

96
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:14,820
Dear.

97
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:16,800
Hey, why did you grow up

98
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:18,770
to be so shameless, sweetheart?

99
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:19,690
Ugh!

100
00:03:20,030 --> 00:03:22,260
Stop touching my face already,
you Grade B supporting actor.

101
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:23,490
Whoa, that's harsh.

102
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:26,140
Hey,

103
00:03:26,230 --> 00:03:27,460
we have to talk to the director

104
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:29,210
in case she knows Grandma Gaysorn.

105
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:33,010
Ugh!

106
00:03:33,030 --> 00:03:35,300
Why is our meeting

107
00:03:35,630 --> 00:03:38,390
so full of obstacles?!

108
00:03:38,810 --> 00:03:42,720
"It is as if the heavens are tormenting us.

109
00:03:43,420 --> 00:03:47,900
With no way out of this anguish,
put up with it we musk.

110
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:52,010
It is not easy to improvise poems, you see?

111
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:57,130
Writer's block has befallen me.
Oh, how I wish to be free."

112
00:03:58,140 --> 00:04:00,630
Gaysorn, where are you?!

113
00:04:11,210 --> 00:04:14,760
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

114
00:04:14,780 --> 00:04:18,560
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

115
00:04:21,110 --> 00:04:26,860
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

116
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:32,980
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

117
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:41,540
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

118
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:46,980
♫One day, we'll find
what we're yearning for♫

119
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:50,630
♫Walking alone is fine,
but it's better when you're by my side♫

120
00:04:50,630 --> 00:04:54,220
♫It won't be lonely
when you're here to walk beside♫

121
00:04:54,220 --> 00:04:57,140
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

122
00:04:57,790 --> 00:05:00,270
♫Like a love that remains,
remains at the dorm♫

123
00:05:00,270 --> 00:05:06,730
♫Meaningful love and good things
await on every path♫

124
00:05:07,170 --> 00:05:13,850
♫It might not be a coincidence
that we get to meet♫

125
00:05:14,370 --> 00:05:21,520
♫There might be hidden meanings
on the path beneath our feet♫

126
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:28,770
♫Perhaps the D Dorm
is what led me to meet you♫

127
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:32,580
[The D Dorm]

128
00:05:32,590 --> 00:05:34,150
[The D Dorm]

129
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:35,700
Oh, where's Handyman Daeng?

130
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:37,420
Didn't he say he'd go to
the nursing home with us?

131
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:39,300
Oh, he went to get some coffee
at Mr. Drip's cafe.

132
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:40,409
I see.

133
00:05:40,430 --> 00:05:41,120
Oh, there he is.

134
00:05:41,140 --> 00:05:41,670
Oh.

135
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:45,500
Hey, what is he carrying?

136
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:49,420
Okay.

137
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:51,350
I'm ready...

138
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:53,310
Whoa.

139
00:05:53,330 --> 00:05:54,420
Look at you.

140
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:56,260
Were you up all night or something?

141
00:05:56,430 --> 00:05:57,620
Last night,

142
00:05:58,030 --> 00:06:00,420
Dawin had me holding his hand

143
00:06:00,450 --> 00:06:02,000
while we looked for Gramps' ghost all night.

144
00:06:02,020 --> 00:06:03,020
Until 5 A.M.

145
00:06:04,060 --> 00:06:06,460
Wow, you two used to fight all the time,

146
00:06:06,610 --> 00:06:11,450
but now you're walking around
holding hands all night, huh?

147
00:06:12,460 --> 00:06:13,330
Oops...

148
00:06:13,770 --> 00:06:15,220
You're getting mad
over just a little teasing?

149
00:06:16,950 --> 00:06:17,940
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

150
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:18,600
I'm good, I'm good!

151
00:06:18,610 --> 00:06:20,720
All good, all good, all good...

152
00:06:20,740 --> 00:06:21,940
Daeng, you're falling asleep standing up.

153
00:06:21,950 --> 00:06:23,020
Why don't you go to bed?

154
00:06:35,510 --> 00:06:36,909
Alright, I'm ready.

155
00:06:38,159 --> 00:06:38,870
Hey,

156
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:40,330
don't get your hopes up.

157
00:06:40,350 --> 00:06:41,480
To be honest,

158
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:43,970
I'm not even sure
if she'll remember anything.

159
00:06:43,990 --> 00:06:45,190
She even mistook me

160
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:47,380
for a friend her age.

161
00:06:47,610 --> 00:06:48,610
Hm...

162
00:06:48,630 --> 00:06:49,900
Maybe it's because you look old?

163
00:06:50,430 --> 00:06:53,630
Yeah? You asking for an earful, huh?

164
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:55,940
I was...reading Guard Dum's thoughts.

165
00:06:55,970 --> 00:06:57,140
Guard Dum, were you thinking out loud?

166
00:06:57,300 --> 00:06:59,220
Your mother looks young enough
to be your age.

167
00:06:59,810 --> 00:07:00,810
That's right.

168
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:02,180
Let's say

169
00:07:02,420 --> 00:07:03,920
the OD doesn't remember anything...

170
00:07:03,940 --> 00:07:04,630
Hm?

171
00:07:04,780 --> 00:07:05,780
- What's "OD"?
- Who's that?

172
00:07:06,530 --> 00:07:07,420
The orphanage director.

173
00:07:07,710 --> 00:07:08,850
- Oh.
- I see.

174
00:07:08,870 --> 00:07:11,300
How are we gonna find
Grandma Gaysorn after this?

175
00:07:14,390 --> 00:07:16,330
I guess I'll have to light some incense
and tell Grandpa

176
00:07:16,690 --> 00:07:19,270
to let go and reincarnate already.

177
00:07:21,320 --> 00:07:22,940
I do not want to!

178
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:24,820
I am not going anywhere.

179
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:26,820
You have to find Gaysorn.

180
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:29,100
If you do not find her,

181
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:32,650
I will stick to you like
a tick on a dog forever.

182
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:34,830
Whoa.

183
00:07:36,140 --> 00:07:37,310
Hello.

184
00:07:37,530 --> 00:07:38,730
We're on our way.

185
00:07:39,830 --> 00:07:41,210
- Huh?!
- Hm? Huh? Huh?

186
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:42,820
I'll be right there!

187
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:44,409
Alright, yes.

188
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:46,740
Her caregiver called

189
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:48,230
and said my mother had disappeared.

190
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:50,300
They looked everywhere
but couldn't find her.

191
00:07:50,520 --> 00:07:51,620
Hey, calm down.

192
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:52,920
She's quite old,

193
00:07:53,420 --> 00:07:54,270
so she can't have gone far.

194
00:07:54,370 --> 00:07:55,320
We'll help you look for her.

195
00:07:55,460 --> 00:07:57,180
How about this?
Go report it to the police first.

196
00:07:57,420 --> 00:07:59,610
I'll wait for Dax,
then join you in the search.

197
00:08:00,110 --> 00:08:00,820
Sounds good?

198
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:01,750
Okay.

199
00:08:01,770 --> 00:08:03,500
- Let's go.
- Go, go, go, go.

200
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:05,220
- Ugh! Come on, Guard Dum.
- Mm, that guy's still asleep.

201
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:06,630
Daeng, come on!

202
00:08:06,650 --> 00:08:07,330
Hurry.

203
00:08:07,860 --> 00:08:09,740
♫Daeng is a fighter♫

204
00:08:10,460 --> 00:08:11,210
Ugh...

205
00:08:12,430 --> 00:08:14,180
Ugh...what's taking him so long?!

206
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:15,000
It is already this late.

207
00:08:15,020 --> 00:08:16,510
Oh, here he is.

208
00:08:17,730 --> 00:08:18,490
So?

209
00:08:18,510 --> 00:08:19,250
Sorry, sorry.

210
00:08:19,270 --> 00:08:21,210
I was looking for a way
to help the director regain her memory.

211
00:08:21,340 --> 00:08:22,260
I found a way

212
00:08:22,430 --> 00:08:23,220
thanks to the Ex.

213
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:24,230
Expert?

214
00:08:24,250 --> 00:08:25,080
Extension cord.

215
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:26,350
It actually works.

216
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:28,060
After I took a shower this morning,

217
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:28,860
I got an electric shock

218
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:30,460
when I plugged in my hair dryer
to blow-dry my hair.

219
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:32,539
Memories came rushing back to me.

220
00:08:32,559 --> 00:08:33,789
My dad's and my mom's faces

221
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:35,260
flashed...through my mind.

222
00:08:35,289 --> 00:08:37,740
Oh, so you'll shock the director
with that extension cord.

223
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:39,220
Yes, in case Grandma Gaysorn's face

224
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:41,130
appears...
in her memories, too.

225
00:08:41,150 --> 00:08:43,370
It appears...you might be sent to jail.

226
00:08:43,390 --> 00:08:44,620
Are you crazy?

227
00:08:44,820 --> 00:08:46,420
Get in the car. Everyone's already left.

228
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:47,030
Hurry!

229
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:48,980
Oh...

230
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:50,100
Wait.

231
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:04,500
[Dohyun, occupation: Korean fortune teller]

232
00:09:04,730 --> 00:09:07,260
Why is this ice cream seller
dressed like that?

233
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:09,230
It is like he is from the Joseon era.

234
00:09:09,330 --> 00:09:11,580
I have cleansed
all the negative energy, Mr. Delta.

235
00:09:20,530 --> 00:09:23,430
[Delta, occupation: businessman]

236
00:09:23,940 --> 00:09:24,940
Stop!

237
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:28,300
Mr. Delta, since this is our first visit
to your new business,

238
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:30,420
you must always step in

239
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:32,060
with your left foot first for good luck.

240
00:09:33,550 --> 00:09:35,220
- Tank you...
- Hey!

241
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:35,860
That is my rhrine.

242
00:09:36,010 --> 00:09:37,230
Thank you for warning me, Dohyun.

243
00:09:44,950 --> 00:09:46,480
- Whoa...
- Oh... The way he walks.

244
00:09:46,550 --> 00:09:47,690
Hello, Mr. Dobby.

245
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:50,780
Do we...know each other?

246
00:09:50,930 --> 00:09:52,820
My name is Delta.

247
00:09:53,230 --> 00:09:55,860
My father is the one
who's going to buy this dorm from you.

248
00:09:56,540 --> 00:09:57,540
I see.

249
00:09:58,020 --> 00:09:58,820
And this is

250
00:09:59,020 --> 00:09:59,780
Dohyun,

251
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:00,910
my personal fortune teller.

252
00:10:01,330 --> 00:10:01,900
Herro.

253
00:10:01,920 --> 00:10:02,920
What halo? I'm not dead.

254
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:05,300
What can I do for you, Mr. Delta?

255
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:06,820
My fortune teller said

256
00:10:07,210 --> 00:10:09,540
my auspicious item is here in this dorm.

257
00:10:09,930 --> 00:10:12,670
That's why I came here to look for it.

258
00:10:12,690 --> 00:10:13,540
Uh...

259
00:10:13,560 --> 00:10:14,480
Could you come another day?

260
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:15,730
He cannot!

261
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:18,610
Hey, he's acting crazy.

262
00:10:20,020 --> 00:10:20,950
Tomorrow

263
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:23,220
is the Sacred Phoenix's birthday!

264
00:10:23,620 --> 00:10:24,600
Mr. Delta

265
00:10:24,610 --> 00:10:27,810
will have to find everyone
who possesses a piece of the phoenix.

266
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,740
Right now, he already has the head,

267
00:10:29,930 --> 00:10:30,620
shoulders,

268
00:10:30,810 --> 00:10:31,410
- Knees.
- knees.

269
00:10:31,430 --> 00:10:31,970
- Hey!
- Hey!

270
00:10:32,660 --> 00:10:33,930
I wanted to say that

271
00:10:34,030 --> 00:10:35,390
the shoulder part is unnecessary.

272
00:10:35,410 --> 00:10:36,720
Do Koreans know this joke, too?

273
00:10:36,750 --> 00:10:37,550
I just found that out, too.

274
00:10:38,310 --> 00:10:39,260
What are the body parts?

275
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:40,820
There have to be a head,

276
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:42,590
- wings,
- Wings.

277
00:10:42,610 --> 00:10:44,150
- a tail,
- A tail.

278
00:10:44,170 --> 00:10:45,390
- and claws.
- Claws.

279
00:10:45,410 --> 00:10:47,530
There is only one part missing.

280
00:10:47,550 --> 00:10:48,380
That is...

281
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:48,920
The heart?

282
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:49,600
The appendix.

283
00:10:49,620 --> 00:10:50,350
- Huh?
- Hm?

284
00:10:50,620 --> 00:10:51,620
Why is the appendix crucial?

285
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:53,070
The appendix is an extra part.

286
00:10:53,090 --> 00:10:54,860
The symbol of imperfection.

287
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:56,090
Yet it is needed.

288
00:10:57,310 --> 00:10:59,820
Just as there is yin, there must be yang.

289
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:01,520
The appendix maintains the balance.

290
00:11:02,740 --> 00:11:03,820
Let's not waste our time, Dohyun.

291
00:11:04,660 --> 00:11:06,580
Let's go find the phoenix's appendix.

292
00:11:06,620 --> 00:11:07,240
Yes.

293
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:13,740
Whoa!

294
00:11:15,220 --> 00:11:16,130
I'll go, too.

295
00:11:16,150 --> 00:11:16,820
Hey.

296
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,220
Don't go.

297
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:19,720
Grandpah, how 'bout this?

298
00:11:21,230 --> 00:11:22,230
Oh, now I'm confused.

299
00:11:22,250 --> 00:11:23,140
- Grandpa, how about this?
- Mm.

300
00:11:23,170 --> 00:11:24,820
You go help Ms. Danis
find the director first.

301
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,300
We'll stay behind to handle those two.

302
00:11:26,430 --> 00:11:28,070
If we let them stay here,

303
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:29,710
the tenants are bound to find out

304
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:30,700
I'm planning to sell the dorm.

305
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:31,430
Okye.

306
00:11:31,450 --> 00:11:32,360
Huh?!

307
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:33,790
- Okay.
- Mm.

308
00:11:33,810 --> 00:11:35,960
Hurry up. And be careful.

309
00:11:35,980 --> 00:11:37,180
If those two

310
00:11:37,310 --> 00:11:39,320
cannot find the phoenix's appendix,

311
00:11:39,340 --> 00:11:43,130
they will turn you into
the phoenix's hemorrhoid.

312
00:11:44,330 --> 00:11:45,280
Just thinking about it hurts.

313
00:11:45,300 --> 00:11:45,970
What hurts?

314
00:11:45,990 --> 00:11:47,120
Hemorrhoids, obviously.
Didn't you hear?

315
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:47,700
I didn't hear anything.

316
00:11:48,630 --> 00:11:49,820
Oh, I was talking to Grandpa. I forgot.

317
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:50,410
Oh.

318
00:11:52,530 --> 00:11:56,710
The wind shall guide me!

319
00:11:58,900 --> 00:12:02,580
The wind shall empower me!

320
00:12:02,830 --> 00:12:04,440
Whee...

321
00:12:05,030 --> 00:12:06,920
Woo...

322
00:12:07,420 --> 00:12:08,540
Whee...

323
00:12:08,550 --> 00:12:11,980
- We...
- We...

324
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:12,670
- Will...
- Will...

325
00:12:12,690 --> 00:12:15,350
♫We will, we will rock you♫

326
00:12:15,370 --> 00:12:18,000
♫We will, we will rock you♫

327
00:12:18,020 --> 00:12:19,020
♫We will, we will find the appendix♫

328
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:19,910
Hey!

329
00:12:20,820 --> 00:12:21,740
The word just fit.

330
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:22,700
How's it going?

331
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:24,130
Did you find the phoenix's appendix?

332
00:12:24,330 --> 00:12:26,090
If you can't find it,
you can come back another day.

333
00:12:26,110 --> 00:12:26,590
This way.

334
00:12:26,610 --> 00:12:27,060
This way...

335
00:12:34,930 --> 00:12:35,930
Dohyun, what's wrong?

336
00:12:38,540 --> 00:12:39,170
Ants.

337
00:12:39,190 --> 00:12:39,990
The ants bit me.

338
00:12:40,130 --> 00:12:42,170
There... There are so many ants over there.

339
00:12:42,190 --> 00:12:43,220
- Ugh.
- Ugh.

340
00:12:43,250 --> 00:12:44,890
Mr. Delta, do not fret.

341
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:46,100
I can sense that

342
00:12:46,210 --> 00:12:49,100
the phoenix's appendix
will surely make an appearance.

343
00:12:49,120 --> 00:12:49,980
- Oh.
- Oh.

344
00:12:50,830 --> 00:12:51,850
Whoa!

345
00:12:51,870 --> 00:12:53,510
There are a lot of you today.
What can I get you?

346
00:12:56,330 --> 00:12:57,380
- Oh!
- Oh!

347
00:12:57,460 --> 00:12:58,380
The phoenix's appendix.

348
00:12:58,400 --> 00:12:59,550
Stir-fried or deep-fried?

349
00:12:59,580 --> 00:13:00,340
- Hey!
- Hey!

350
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:01,830
I sell made-to-order food,

351
00:13:01,850 --> 00:13:02,630
not foraged food.

352
00:13:03,010 --> 00:13:04,540
What do you mean, appendix?

353
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:05,420
Dohyun,

354
00:13:05,930 --> 00:13:07,380
are you sure that's
the phoenix's appendix?

355
00:13:07,410 --> 00:13:08,980
She looks more like adrenal glands to me.

356
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:10,750
Who are these two?

357
00:13:11,310 --> 00:13:12,830
Why are you calling me adrenal glands, huh?

358
00:13:12,950 --> 00:13:14,110
Hello, I'm Delta.

359
00:13:14,130 --> 00:13:15,510
- I came here to buy...
- Buy?

360
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:17,360
Buy...food from your place.

361
00:13:17,390 --> 00:13:19,070
Red curry, chicken curry, eel curry, chu chee,

362
00:13:19,090 --> 00:13:20,300
massaman curry, stir-fried noodles, yellow curry,

363
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:22,410
and poh...teak!

364
00:13:22,420 --> 00:13:25,060
Wow! If they're ordering this much,
call me adrenal glands,

365
00:13:25,090 --> 00:13:26,960
or even a wart on my big toe.

366
00:13:27,550 --> 00:13:28,170
Just a sec.

367
00:13:28,190 --> 00:13:29,120
Please wait.

368
00:13:29,140 --> 00:13:29,740
- Yes.
- Thank you.

369
00:13:30,030 --> 00:13:30,740
Mm.

370
00:13:33,120 --> 00:13:33,810
Hey,

371
00:13:34,340 --> 00:13:35,420
what are you gonna do with her?

372
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:36,720
I'm not going to do anything to her.

373
00:13:36,740 --> 00:13:37,980
I just want to ask her to work for me.

374
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:39,120
That is right.

375
00:13:39,140 --> 00:13:41,310
To enhance Mr. Delta's fortune and prestige,

376
00:13:42,020 --> 00:13:44,530
it is essential that someone
born under the Phoenix sign

377
00:13:44,550 --> 00:13:47,370
serve as one of his subordinates,
working close by his side.

378
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:48,060
Ugh...

379
00:13:48,460 --> 00:13:49,460
- She's not going anywhere.
- Mm.

380
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,860
She loves her kids to death.

381
00:13:50,880 --> 00:13:51,330
That's right.

382
00:13:51,350 --> 00:13:52,770
She wouldn't leave them behind.

383
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:53,490
Mm.

384
00:13:53,620 --> 00:13:55,120
Think she'll still be able to resist

385
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:57,860
a house and
a monthly salary of 300,000 baht?

386
00:13:58,510 --> 00:13:59,320
300,000?!

387
00:14:00,030 --> 00:14:01,100
Whoa. Uh...excuse me.

388
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:02,230
Could you check my birth fortune, too?

389
00:14:02,340 --> 00:14:04,300
Maybe I'm the phoenix's butt hair.

390
00:14:04,430 --> 00:14:05,990
Ugh! Dax!

391
00:14:06,170 --> 00:14:06,770
What?

392
00:14:06,930 --> 00:14:07,740
Hey,

393
00:14:07,770 --> 00:14:08,780
she's not going anywhere.

394
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:11,300
If you're offering her
a house and money like that,

395
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:12,200
she's certainly not gonna leave.

396
00:14:12,220 --> 00:14:13,070
She doesn't like rich people

397
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:14,900
who think they can win
others over with money.

398
00:14:14,980 --> 00:14:17,000
But you only ordered a few dishes,

399
00:14:17,230 --> 00:14:18,960
and she became a wart on the big toe.

400
00:14:20,230 --> 00:14:20,890
Hey,

401
00:14:21,520 --> 00:14:22,580
she was just joking.

402
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:24,030
She wouldn't agree to that.

403
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:25,300
How about this?

404
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:27,210
If you really want Auntie Duang
to work with you,

405
00:14:27,820 --> 00:14:29,120
I can try to persuade her.

406
00:14:30,040 --> 00:14:32,460
Because the tenants haven't come to terms

407
00:14:32,620 --> 00:14:34,120
with having to leave this dorm yet.

408
00:14:34,270 --> 00:14:36,610
And if they find out
your father is gonna buy this dorm...

409
00:14:36,630 --> 00:14:38,020
Oh, that'll break their hearts.

410
00:14:39,630 --> 00:14:40,630
Is that alright with you?

411
00:14:41,910 --> 00:14:42,510
Okay.

412
00:14:42,620 --> 00:14:43,620
Dobby, Dobby,

413
00:14:44,050 --> 00:14:45,220
- come here.
- What?

414
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:47,450
How are you gonna
tell this to Auntie Duang?

415
00:14:47,470 --> 00:14:49,140
Come on, I've got a way to handle this.

416
00:14:49,230 --> 00:14:50,620
Even if we sell this dorm,

417
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:51,940
she'll have to close her place anyway.

418
00:14:52,420 --> 00:14:53,190
At least

419
00:14:53,210 --> 00:14:55,460
we could help her find
a way to support herself.

420
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:57,120
Listen,

421
00:14:57,140 --> 00:14:59,320
keep an eye on those two.

422
00:14:59,630 --> 00:15:02,510
Don't let them tell anyone
about the dorm purchase,

423
00:15:02,710 --> 00:15:03,280
alright?

424
00:15:03,520 --> 00:15:04,200
Okay.

425
00:15:06,380 --> 00:15:06,910
- Oh...
- Oh...

426
00:15:08,830 --> 00:15:09,960
- Okay...
- Okay?

427
00:15:09,980 --> 00:15:11,750
Is that alright, Mr. Delta?

428
00:15:15,140 --> 00:15:16,220
Excuse me,

429
00:15:16,660 --> 00:15:19,110
have you seen
this woman in this photo around here?

430
00:15:19,310 --> 00:15:20,530
No, I haven't.

431
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:22,920
Watch out...

432
00:15:22,970 --> 00:15:24,360
Oh, Guard Dum.

433
00:15:24,380 --> 00:15:26,190
Why are you just pushing that cart around?

434
00:15:26,210 --> 00:15:27,840
Why aren't you helping me
look for my mother?

435
00:15:28,020 --> 00:15:29,990
I'm not pushing it around for fun.
I'm pushing a sleeping person.

436
00:15:30,660 --> 00:15:31,440
Whoa!

437
00:15:31,460 --> 00:15:32,190
Handyman Daeng.

438
00:15:33,380 --> 00:15:34,600
Whoa! I found her!

439
00:15:34,620 --> 00:15:36,100
I found the director!

440
00:15:36,120 --> 00:15:37,150
Where? Where is she?

441
00:15:37,740 --> 00:15:38,950
I... I found her in my dreams.

442
00:15:38,970 --> 00:15:39,660
Ugh...

443
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:41,730
Not only are you not helping,
you're being a burden.

444
00:15:43,920 --> 00:15:45,060
- Oh, oh.
- Oh, be careful.

445
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:46,500
Don't say that.

446
00:15:46,530 --> 00:15:47,790
I'm trying my best here.

447
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:49,920
I was looking for her

448
00:15:50,220 --> 00:15:51,460
even in my dreams.

449
00:15:52,970 --> 00:15:55,320
The police haven't made any progress either.

450
00:15:56,740 --> 00:15:57,230
Let's go.

451
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:58,560
Let's look for her together.

452
00:15:58,820 --> 00:15:59,450
- Hey!
- Ow.

453
00:15:59,470 --> 00:16:00,070
Whoa.

454
00:16:00,230 --> 00:16:02,140
Why did you steal my sports car?

455
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:03,580
What sports car?

456
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:04,620
This!

457
00:16:04,740 --> 00:16:06,350
The Must-have sports car.

458
00:16:06,370 --> 00:16:07,690
It's the real deal.

459
00:16:08,540 --> 00:16:09,260
Hey...

460
00:16:09,420 --> 00:16:10,780
He's that madman living near our dorm.

461
00:16:10,810 --> 00:16:12,300
Madman, my foot.

462
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:13,800
He came all the way here?

463
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:16,650
Hello, beautiful.

464
00:16:16,710 --> 00:16:19,250
Wanna go for a ride in my sports car?

465
00:16:25,980 --> 00:16:26,620
Hey!

466
00:16:30,140 --> 00:16:32,110
That's my mother's shawl!

467
00:16:32,380 --> 00:16:32,990
Really?

468
00:16:33,210 --> 00:16:34,120
Hey, give it to me!

469
00:16:34,150 --> 00:16:34,820
Hey!

470
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:35,460
What the heck?

471
00:16:35,470 --> 00:16:36,090
Hey!

472
00:16:36,110 --> 00:16:37,730
Don't you dare touch my car, red panda.

473
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:39,830
Please calm down.

474
00:16:39,850 --> 00:16:42,100
We're not going to do anything to your car.

475
00:16:42,240 --> 00:16:43,180
I just want to ask...

476
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:45,080
where did you get that shawl?

477
00:16:45,100 --> 00:16:46,410
You really wanna know?

478
00:16:46,930 --> 00:16:47,740
If you wanna know,

479
00:16:47,750 --> 00:16:49,910
why don't you come for a spin with me?

480
00:16:50,250 --> 00:16:50,910
A spin...

481
00:16:51,850 --> 00:16:52,880
Be careful, Ms. Danis.

482
00:16:52,890 --> 00:16:53,800
I remember now.

483
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:54,850
This madman

484
00:16:54,870 --> 00:16:56,240
once chased Mr. Drip

485
00:16:56,330 --> 00:16:58,180
and hurt his leg so badly
he ended up in the hospital.

486
00:16:58,820 --> 00:17:00,830
But if we find out where he got that shawl,

487
00:17:00,850 --> 00:17:02,650
it'll be easier to look for my mother.

488
00:17:02,670 --> 00:17:04,650
Hey, we're talking about a madman here.

489
00:17:04,670 --> 00:17:06,430
"Madman," my foot! I'm not crazy.

490
00:17:07,230 --> 00:17:08,329
He's not right in the head.

491
00:17:08,349 --> 00:17:09,760
Now that sounds a lot better.

492
00:17:11,230 --> 00:17:12,230
Uh...

493
00:17:12,380 --> 00:17:13,910
It's broad daylight.
We'll probably be fine.

494
00:17:16,020 --> 00:17:17,690
Hey, handsome.

495
00:17:17,940 --> 00:17:19,460
Yes, beautiful?

496
00:17:19,490 --> 00:17:21,650
I want to ask you something.

497
00:17:21,670 --> 00:17:22,710
But on one condition.

498
00:17:22,730 --> 00:17:25,859
You have to come for a little ride with me.

499
00:17:26,740 --> 00:17:28,610
Right this way. I'll open the door for you.

500
00:17:31,660 --> 00:17:32,890
Is that a door or a coffin opening?

501
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:33,820
A door, obviously.

502
00:17:34,940 --> 00:17:35,620
Hop in.

503
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:37,660
Okay.

504
00:17:37,830 --> 00:17:38,830
Come, come.

505
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:40,220
- Yes, thank you...
- Hop in.

506
00:17:40,240 --> 00:17:41,650
Thank you.

507
00:17:43,450 --> 00:17:44,900
- Be careful, alright?
- Yes.

508
00:17:44,930 --> 00:17:46,230
The seat might bounce.

509
00:17:48,130 --> 00:17:49,130
- Ow, ow!
- Whoa!

510
00:17:49,310 --> 00:17:50,100
- What?
- Ow, ow.

511
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:50,960
The door caught my finger.

512
00:17:51,810 --> 00:17:53,010
Not used to a luxury car, huh?

513
00:17:53,980 --> 00:17:55,580
[The D Dorm]

514
00:17:56,710 --> 00:17:57,730
How am I gonna convince her

515
00:17:57,750 --> 00:18:00,200
to be the phoenix's appendix for Mr. Delta?

516
00:18:01,430 --> 00:18:02,600
Should I come up with something?

517
00:18:02,710 --> 00:18:03,980
What are you planning to tell her?

518
00:18:04,220 --> 00:18:05,020
I'm not.

519
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:06,720
Huh? Who was that?

520
00:18:13,510 --> 00:18:14,200
What are you doing?

521
00:18:14,230 --> 00:18:17,010
I'm training for
the HYROX competition with Dollar.

522
00:18:18,540 --> 00:18:19,430
Hope you come in first.

523
00:18:19,460 --> 00:18:20,480
- Thank you so much.
- Mm...

524
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:21,510
Hey, wait.

525
00:18:21,530 --> 00:18:21,920
Hm?

526
00:18:21,940 --> 00:18:23,650
I heard what you said earlier, Mr. Dobby.

527
00:18:23,670 --> 00:18:24,810
Are you planning to trick Auntie Duang?

528
00:18:24,820 --> 00:18:25,670
Spill the beans.

529
00:18:26,410 --> 00:18:27,430
This is between the adults.

530
00:18:27,770 --> 00:18:28,560
Stay out of it, alright?

531
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:30,750
I can't stay out of it.

532
00:18:30,770 --> 00:18:32,940
If anything happens to Dollar's mom,

533
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:35,910
how's he supposed to have the heart
to compete in HYROX with me?

534
00:18:35,930 --> 00:18:37,470
So answer me, Mr. Dobby,

535
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:39,700
- are you planning to trick Auntie Duang?
- Hm!

536
00:18:39,940 --> 00:18:41,330
Who? Who's trying to trick me?

537
00:18:43,310 --> 00:18:44,820
No one, Auntie Duang.

538
00:18:45,140 --> 00:18:47,320
Well...my friend

539
00:18:47,340 --> 00:18:48,220
got scammed by his housemaid,

540
00:18:48,330 --> 00:18:49,700
so he's looking for a new one.

541
00:18:49,810 --> 00:18:51,500
He's offering 300,000 baht!

542
00:18:51,520 --> 00:18:52,320
300,000?!

543
00:18:52,340 --> 00:18:53,540
That's right.

544
00:18:53,560 --> 00:18:55,390
Is he looking for a housemaid
or a mistress?

545
00:18:56,030 --> 00:18:56,720
Hey, Dobby.

546
00:18:56,730 --> 00:18:58,560
I may look alluring,

547
00:18:58,580 --> 00:19:00,790
but I still have my dignity.

548
00:19:00,810 --> 00:19:02,040
Oh, I think intimidating is the right word.

549
00:19:02,060 --> 00:19:03,530
Just kidding.

550
00:19:03,740 --> 00:19:04,860
It's not like that, Auntie Duang.

551
00:19:04,970 --> 00:19:06,300
He really is looking for a housemaid.

552
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:07,510
My friend is loaded,

553
00:19:07,530 --> 00:19:09,000
and he's taken a liking to you.

554
00:19:09,220 --> 00:19:10,630
That's why he wants you

555
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:11,910
to work with him

556
00:19:12,140 --> 00:19:13,450
and bring him good fortune.

557
00:19:14,220 --> 00:19:14,840
Whoa...

558
00:19:14,860 --> 00:19:15,580
Yes.

559
00:19:15,600 --> 00:19:16,530
That sounds interesting.

560
00:19:16,540 --> 00:19:17,270
Yeah!

561
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:20,250
Don't fall for it yet, Auntie.

562
00:19:20,270 --> 00:19:21,850
Listen to me carefully.

563
00:19:21,930 --> 00:19:22,720
Huh?

564
00:19:23,510 --> 00:19:24,730
Oh... Whoa.

565
00:19:25,830 --> 00:19:27,780
He's using 300,000 baht to lure you in.

566
00:19:29,700 --> 00:19:30,700
There's no doubt...

567
00:19:31,020 --> 00:19:31,810
Ugh...

568
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:33,920
He must be a scammer.

569
00:19:34,230 --> 00:19:35,630
Hm...

570
00:19:36,420 --> 00:19:37,880
He isn't!

571
00:19:39,940 --> 00:19:40,670
If he's not,

572
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:42,310
where does he get 300,000 baht from?

573
00:19:42,610 --> 00:19:43,580
Yeah.

574
00:19:44,350 --> 00:19:45,250
I think...

575
00:19:45,270 --> 00:19:47,430
he's tricking you into selling your organs!

576
00:19:47,450 --> 00:19:48,510
Whoa...

577
00:19:50,020 --> 00:19:51,370
If you don't believe me,

578
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:52,540
you can talk to him first.

579
00:19:55,660 --> 00:19:56,250
Let's go.

580
00:19:57,760 --> 00:19:58,550
You want to meet my friend?

581
00:19:58,570 --> 00:19:59,570
I want to see a doctor.

582
00:19:59,590 --> 00:20:00,160
Huh?

583
00:20:00,180 --> 00:20:02,580
My knees hurt.
My legs can't take this anymore.

584
00:20:03,430 --> 00:20:06,330
Dobby, if you want me to talk
to your friend,

585
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:08,750
can you wait until
Dollar gets back from work?

586
00:20:08,780 --> 00:20:10,880
I feel more comfortable when I have

587
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:12,110
a cop with me.

588
00:20:12,130 --> 00:20:13,540
Come on...

589
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:14,640
Are you gonna send Dollar

590
00:20:14,660 --> 00:20:16,490
to do aerobics in front of the scammers?

591
00:20:16,510 --> 00:20:17,860
Attention!

592
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:19,290
Present arms!

593
00:20:19,580 --> 00:20:20,740
Okay, please follow along.

594
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:23,730
Right, left, right, left,

595
00:20:23,750 --> 00:20:25,300
right. Ow...my back.

596
00:20:25,620 --> 00:20:27,850
I'm screwed. If Dollar comes with us,

597
00:20:27,870 --> 00:20:29,900
they'll find out I'm selling this dorm.

598
00:20:29,920 --> 00:20:31,210
What should I do?

599
00:20:31,710 --> 00:20:32,560
[DO-MUN-DRIP]

600
00:20:47,910 --> 00:20:50,460
Why does he have to look so cool
just smelling coffee?

601
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:05,820
How is that cool?

602
00:21:06,320 --> 00:21:07,650
He looks like he's sniffing glue.

603
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:10,930
This is good stuff.
It really hits the spot.

604
00:21:12,130 --> 00:21:12,910
Uh...

605
00:21:13,130 --> 00:21:13,990
Mr. Dolly,

606
00:21:14,710 --> 00:21:16,990
could you give this a sniff...

607
00:21:17,010 --> 00:21:18,570
and tell me if it's over-roasted?

608
00:21:19,500 --> 00:21:20,490
Of course.

609
00:21:40,990 --> 00:21:41,990
Whoa!

610
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:44,740
It smells so good.

611
00:21:47,750 --> 00:21:50,660
Then...I'll order more of this next time.

612
00:21:53,510 --> 00:21:55,220
Now that that's settled.

613
00:21:56,250 --> 00:21:57,310
Who called for them?

614
00:22:03,730 --> 00:22:05,530
I have eradicated all negative energy.

615
00:22:13,860 --> 00:22:14,630
Mr. Dax,

616
00:22:15,120 --> 00:22:16,720
who are you bringing into my cafe?

617
00:22:16,840 --> 00:22:17,530
Oh,

618
00:22:18,040 --> 00:22:18,980
they're Dobby's friends.

619
00:22:19,260 --> 00:22:20,000
I brought them here for coffee.

620
00:22:20,980 --> 00:22:22,400
Why is he walking like that, though?

621
00:22:23,390 --> 00:22:24,340
Or does he have a disability?

622
00:22:24,360 --> 00:22:25,230
Silence!

623
00:22:25,580 --> 00:22:27,420
Do not look down on my ritual.

624
00:22:27,620 --> 00:22:29,850
This walk is meant to bring good fortune.

625
00:22:30,540 --> 00:22:31,580
How about some shoe lifts first?

626
00:22:31,930 --> 00:22:34,100
At this rate,
you'll wear your heels right down.

627
00:22:34,260 --> 00:22:35,710
How dare you?!

628
00:22:36,140 --> 00:22:36,930
Calm down.

629
00:22:36,950 --> 00:22:38,370
Delta believes in that sort of thing,

630
00:22:38,390 --> 00:22:40,840
and Dohyun is a Korean fortune teller.

631
00:22:43,180 --> 00:22:44,990
Oh...

632
00:22:45,020 --> 00:22:46,930
He said starting off on your left foot

633
00:22:46,960 --> 00:22:48,050
would bring you good luck.

634
00:22:49,610 --> 00:22:50,610
Delta.

635
00:22:51,420 --> 00:22:53,710
No wonder you look so familiar.

636
00:22:53,730 --> 00:22:54,730
Do you remember me?

637
00:22:55,310 --> 00:22:57,500
I'm Dolly!

638
00:22:58,640 --> 00:22:59,270
Dolly...

639
00:23:02,360 --> 00:23:03,360
Dol...

640
00:23:03,680 --> 00:23:04,950
Dolly Darling?

641
00:23:05,380 --> 00:23:06,310
Yes!

642
00:23:06,320 --> 00:23:07,890
Hey, I thought you had forgotten about me,

643
00:23:07,910 --> 00:23:08,910
Delta Oppa.

644
00:23:10,320 --> 00:23:11,620
Is he your friend, Mr. Dolly?

645
00:23:12,030 --> 00:23:12,760
Yes.

646
00:23:12,880 --> 00:23:14,140
We were friends back in middle school.

647
00:23:15,440 --> 00:23:17,340
One's "Dolly Darling,"

648
00:23:17,630 --> 00:23:19,620
and the other's "Delta Oppa."

649
00:23:19,650 --> 00:23:21,110
They call each other by their nicknames.

650
00:23:21,140 --> 00:23:22,310
Are they really just friends?

651
00:23:24,030 --> 00:23:25,370
If he says they're "friends,"
then they're "friends."

652
00:23:26,060 --> 00:23:27,680
Why do you even want to know?

653
00:23:27,700 --> 00:23:28,700
Ugh!

654
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:29,780
What are you even mad at me for?

655
00:23:31,260 --> 00:23:32,090
I think...

656
00:23:32,110 --> 00:23:34,330
there is still
some negative energy lingering here.

657
00:23:34,600 --> 00:23:35,320
We should...

658
00:23:35,330 --> 00:23:37,670
get coffee somewhere else, Mr. Delta.

659
00:23:38,730 --> 00:23:39,360
It's alright.

660
00:23:40,510 --> 00:23:41,980
Since I'm seeing an old friend,
let's get it here.

661
00:23:44,430 --> 00:23:46,450
Do Korean fortune tellers
crack Thai-style jokes, too?

662
00:23:48,310 --> 00:23:48,970
I missed you.

663
00:24:01,850 --> 00:24:03,120
- Hey, handsome.
- Oh...

664
00:24:03,150 --> 00:24:05,670
When are you going to tell me
where you got that shawl from?

665
00:24:05,690 --> 00:24:06,690
Hey...

666
00:24:06,710 --> 00:24:08,410
I'm driving right now.

667
00:24:08,430 --> 00:24:10,220
I need to condense here.

668
00:24:10,240 --> 00:24:10,930
Concentrate.

669
00:24:10,950 --> 00:24:12,570
Yes, I need to concentrate here.

670
00:24:12,590 --> 00:24:14,600
See this? The gearshift came off.

671
00:24:17,730 --> 00:24:19,320
I've been looking everywhere for you.

672
00:24:19,340 --> 00:24:20,920
So you've been messing around
with this madman, huh?

673
00:24:20,940 --> 00:24:22,670
So? What are you going to do, huh?

674
00:24:22,680 --> 00:24:24,780
Are you going to let him
take you to the director?

675
00:24:25,130 --> 00:24:26,130
Ms. Danis,

676
00:24:26,260 --> 00:24:27,810
I think we should stop here.

677
00:24:28,110 --> 00:24:29,940
We're not gonna get through to him anyway.

678
00:24:30,220 --> 00:24:31,290
He won't tell us anything.

679
00:24:32,020 --> 00:24:32,850
Hey, kid.

680
00:24:32,870 --> 00:24:35,050
If you're here to sell me garlands, scram.

681
00:24:35,310 --> 00:24:36,610
I don't worship any deity

682
00:24:36,630 --> 00:24:37,860
other than...

683
00:24:37,950 --> 00:24:38,540
Other than?

684
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:39,950
Sun Wukong.

685
00:24:41,630 --> 00:24:42,950
Let me handle this.

686
00:24:45,300 --> 00:24:46,960
You poor soul.

687
00:24:46,980 --> 00:24:47,980
Oh.

688
00:24:48,060 --> 00:24:49,780
Do you revere Son Wukong?

689
00:24:49,800 --> 00:24:50,550
That's right.

690
00:24:50,710 --> 00:24:51,920
Then you shall respect me,

691
00:24:51,940 --> 00:24:53,830
for I am greater than Son Wukong.

692
00:24:53,930 --> 00:24:54,640
And you are?

693
00:24:54,660 --> 00:24:55,660
Dad Wukong.

694
00:24:56,200 --> 00:24:57,130
You never disappoint me.

695
00:24:57,150 --> 00:24:59,760
We must hasten to find the Buddha sutrists.

696
00:24:59,780 --> 00:25:00,320
Hey!

697
00:25:00,340 --> 00:25:01,340
Buddhist sutras.

698
00:25:01,860 --> 00:25:02,750
Great Dad Wukong.

699
00:25:02,840 --> 00:25:03,440
Do speak.

700
00:25:03,710 --> 00:25:05,060
What the hell are you talking about?

701
00:25:05,580 --> 00:25:06,810
Are you crazy, red panda?

702
00:25:06,830 --> 00:25:07,710
He knows how to cut you off.

703
00:25:07,730 --> 00:25:09,000
See? He remembers.

704
00:25:09,020 --> 00:25:10,070
Hey, handsome!

705
00:25:10,120 --> 00:25:11,500
Please tell me

706
00:25:11,520 --> 00:25:13,060
where you got that shawl.

707
00:25:13,080 --> 00:25:14,800
It belongs to my mother!

708
00:25:14,820 --> 00:25:17,660
I'm looking for her!

709
00:25:19,870 --> 00:25:22,420
Oh, beautiful.

710
00:25:23,110 --> 00:25:24,440
Don't cry.

711
00:25:25,410 --> 00:25:27,780
I'll tell you the truth.

712
00:25:27,880 --> 00:25:29,130
The truth is...

713
00:25:30,220 --> 00:25:31,680
you're not my type at all.

714
00:25:31,840 --> 00:25:33,050
You're so ugly.

715
00:25:33,160 --> 00:25:35,010
Get out of my Must-have car right now.

716
00:25:35,030 --> 00:25:35,990
Get out!

717
00:25:37,130 --> 00:25:37,940
Fine.

718
00:25:38,830 --> 00:25:40,060
So, that's how you want it, huh,

719
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:41,030
handsome?

720
00:25:41,050 --> 00:25:41,910
- Oh?
- Oh, boy...

721
00:25:42,220 --> 00:25:43,330
She's gonna knock some sense into you.

722
00:25:43,350 --> 00:25:45,530
What's up, ugly?

723
00:25:47,220 --> 00:25:48,290
Battle!

724
00:25:49,140 --> 00:25:50,220
I'll sleep through this one.

725
00:25:51,730 --> 00:25:53,890
You're not gonna tell me, are you?

726
00:25:53,910 --> 00:25:56,420
I only know one word in English.

727
00:25:57,240 --> 00:25:57,750
"No."

728
00:26:02,220 --> 00:26:04,000
- Fine, then.
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.

729
00:26:04,020 --> 00:26:04,770
What are you doing?

730
00:26:05,070 --> 00:26:05,980
Whoa! Hey!

731
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:06,930
Are you gonna tell me?

732
00:26:06,950 --> 00:26:08,170
Stop doing that!

733
00:26:08,190 --> 00:26:10,410
- Don't touch my Must-have car!
- Where did you get that shawl from?!

734
00:26:10,430 --> 00:26:12,020
Are you gonna tell me or not?

735
00:26:12,940 --> 00:26:14,230
Come on, spill it. Tell me!

736
00:26:14,250 --> 00:26:15,780
I'll tell you now. I'll tell you.

737
00:26:15,800 --> 00:26:17,780
Too slow! Where did you get it from?!

738
00:26:17,800 --> 00:26:20,460
I got it from an auntie wearing
a yellow shirt and yellow pants.

739
00:26:20,480 --> 00:26:21,770
An auntie dressed in yellow?

740
00:26:21,790 --> 00:26:23,060
Where is she now?

741
00:26:24,730 --> 00:26:26,230
Toot-toot. Chugga-chugga-chugga.

742
00:26:26,250 --> 00:26:28,280
Toot-toot. Chugga-chugga-chugga.

743
00:26:28,300 --> 00:26:30,210
Toot-toot, toot-toot.

744
00:26:30,230 --> 00:26:33,150
Oh, I know where the director is.

745
00:26:33,580 --> 00:26:34,820
Hm, let me join in.

746
00:26:34,840 --> 00:26:36,680
We shouldn't have wasted so much time
playing along with him.

747
00:26:36,700 --> 00:26:38,720
If you had broken
his Must-not-have car earlier,

748
00:26:38,730 --> 00:26:39,300
we'd be on our way by now!

749
00:26:39,320 --> 00:26:40,810
- Hand it to me.
- Hey, hey, stop!

750
00:26:40,830 --> 00:26:42,720
- I don't care anymore.
- No, no, no, don't.

751
00:26:43,420 --> 00:26:46,120
- Here.
- Now I Must-find a new car.

752
00:26:46,130 --> 00:26:47,210
You'll have to wait,

753
00:26:47,220 --> 00:26:48,540
because growing these takes time.

754
00:26:52,320 --> 00:26:53,220
Die, Bob Ross.

755
00:26:53,630 --> 00:26:54,760
I'm Bob Loss.

756
00:26:55,320 --> 00:26:56,150
Mm.

757
00:27:03,630 --> 00:27:04,630
Director!

758
00:27:05,820 --> 00:27:08,820
Director, where are you? Director!

759
00:27:10,210 --> 00:27:13,030
Director, where are you? Director.

760
00:27:14,220 --> 00:27:15,410
Director!

761
00:27:17,420 --> 00:27:18,220
Oh, found you.

762
00:27:18,230 --> 00:27:20,150
She is wearing yellow. This has to be her.

763
00:27:20,230 --> 00:27:21,000
Danis!

764
00:27:21,020 --> 00:27:22,640
Danis, the director is here!

765
00:27:22,730 --> 00:27:23,740
Danis!

766
00:27:23,930 --> 00:27:24,930
Danai!

767
00:27:54,200 --> 00:27:55,500
Gaysorn!

768
00:27:55,730 --> 00:27:56,920
Danai!

769
00:27:58,240 --> 00:27:59,940
You can see me?

770
00:28:02,030 --> 00:28:03,420
Gaysorn.

771
00:28:04,120 --> 00:28:05,120
Danai.

772
00:28:05,240 --> 00:28:05,860
Danai...

773
00:28:18,850 --> 00:28:19,500
Oh...

774
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:26,420
Gaysorn.

775
00:28:34,530 --> 00:28:35,920
Danai.

776
00:28:36,630 --> 00:28:39,620
You have not forgotten about me.

777
00:28:40,520 --> 00:28:41,920
Neither have I.

778
00:28:42,520 --> 00:28:44,730
I never forgot about you,

779
00:28:45,920 --> 00:28:47,030
Gaysorn.

780
00:29:17,520 --> 00:29:18,310
Mother.

781
00:29:18,330 --> 00:29:19,420
Director.

782
00:29:21,230 --> 00:29:21,830
Mother.

783
00:29:21,850 --> 00:29:22,610
Director.

784
00:29:25,030 --> 00:29:26,030
Mother!

785
00:29:27,690 --> 00:29:28,270
Mother!

786
00:29:28,380 --> 00:29:29,130
Mother!!

787
00:29:29,810 --> 00:29:30,940
Mother...

788
00:29:30,960 --> 00:29:32,260
Mother, are you okay?

789
00:29:32,280 --> 00:29:33,540
Are you hurt?

790
00:29:33,620 --> 00:29:34,910
I'm alright.

791
00:29:34,930 --> 00:29:36,130
I'm fine,

792
00:29:36,150 --> 00:29:37,230
Danis, my dear friend.

793
00:29:38,300 --> 00:29:38,900
Oh.

794
00:29:40,820 --> 00:29:42,000
Oh, are they your children?

795
00:29:42,950 --> 00:29:45,660
Aww, he's so cute and chubby!

796
00:29:46,030 --> 00:29:46,920
Right?

797
00:29:46,940 --> 00:29:49,520
My little brother
is the cutest in the world.

798
00:29:50,060 --> 00:29:51,770
That's right.
I was only recently weaned.

799
00:29:51,780 --> 00:29:52,610
Hey!

800
00:29:52,620 --> 00:29:54,040
This isn't the time
to play along with her, is it?

801
00:29:54,070 --> 00:29:55,920
Um, we'd better head back now,

802
00:29:55,940 --> 00:29:58,380
so we can let the police know
we've found the director.

803
00:29:58,680 --> 00:29:59,690
Let's go, Mother.

804
00:29:59,710 --> 00:30:00,260
No, no, no.

805
00:30:00,270 --> 00:30:01,770
I'm not going anywhere.
I'm staying here.

806
00:30:02,020 --> 00:30:03,500
I'm meeting my boyfriend.

807
00:30:03,530 --> 00:30:04,530
Boyfriend?

808
00:30:05,120 --> 00:30:06,380
Who is your boyfriend?

809
00:30:10,320 --> 00:30:12,200
Look. That's my boyfriend, Danai.

810
00:30:12,620 --> 00:30:13,320
Huh?

811
00:30:18,510 --> 00:30:19,730
And don't tell anyone, okay?

812
00:30:19,750 --> 00:30:20,630
He said

813
00:30:20,650 --> 00:30:23,710
he's taking me with him to Chiang Mai.

814
00:30:25,520 --> 00:30:27,010
My boyfriend, Danai!

815
00:30:27,540 --> 00:30:28,540
Did I see that right?

816
00:30:28,830 --> 00:30:30,690
That's Mr. Dobby on the TV, isn't it?

817
00:30:33,530 --> 00:30:34,500
Danai...

818
00:30:34,730 --> 00:30:36,240
that's Gramps' name.

819
00:30:37,320 --> 00:30:38,320
Don't tell me

820
00:30:38,530 --> 00:30:39,530
the director

821
00:30:41,230 --> 00:30:42,740
is Grandma Gaysorn?

822
00:30:48,180 --> 00:30:50,300
[DO-MUN-DRIP]

823
00:30:51,760 --> 00:30:53,580
Dolly Darling,
you can eat garlic chives now?

824
00:30:54,180 --> 00:30:55,260
Didn't you say you hated the smell?

825
00:30:55,400 --> 00:30:57,530
Delta Oppa, you still remember that?

826
00:30:58,450 --> 00:30:59,430
Maybe because I'm older.

827
00:31:00,100 --> 00:31:01,470
Now I can eat things

828
00:31:01,620 --> 00:31:02,910
I never used to eat.

829
00:31:03,320 --> 00:31:04,830
I can even eat

830
00:31:05,030 --> 00:31:05,950
bitter melons now.

831
00:31:10,250 --> 00:31:11,380
Didn't you say you'd grown up?

832
